## Install

1. Drop the `Scripts/` folder into your project's `Assets/`.
2. Add the `{{ s.name }}` component to any GameObject you want to control with this AI.
{% if s.nav_backend == "navmesh" %}
3. The GameObject also needs a `NavMeshAgent` (auto-required). Bake a NavMesh in the
   scene (Window → AI → Navigation).
{% elif s.nav_backend == "kinematic_2d" %}
3. No NavMesh needed — this is a 2D project, so the AI seeks targets directly via
   `transform.position` in the XY plane (no `NavMeshAgent`, no bake required).
{% endif %}
{% if variant in ("navmesh_patrol", "fsm_guard") %}
4. Create {{ s.patrol_point_count }} empty GameObjects in the scene as patrol points
   and drag them into the `patrolPoints` array in the inspector.
{% endif %}
5. Tag the player GameObject `{{ s.target_tag }}` so the AI can find it.
{% if s.use_health_hook %}
6. Implement a `TakeDamage(float)` method on the player to receive damage from this AI.
{% endif %}

