## Perception

This AI does not have omniscient sight — it notices the target only within a
facing-relative vision cone, blocked by anything between it and the target
(both toggleable), and separately picks up on fast/loud movement (sprinting)
within a hearing radius even when out of sight. Losing the target does not
mean instantly forgetting it: the AI keeps heading for its last known
position for a short memory window before actually giving up.

| Field                 | Default | Notes |
|-----------------------|---------|-------|
| `visionAngle`         | {{ "%.0f"|format(s.vision_angle) }}° | cone width centred on facing; 360 = omniscient sphere |
| `visionObstruction`   | {{ s.vision_obstruction }} | raycast line-of-sight check |
| `eyeHeight`           | {{ "%.1f"|format(s.eye_height) }}m | raycast origin/target height offset |
| `hearingRadius`       | {{ "%.1f"|format(s.hearing_radius) }}m | 0 disables hearing |
| `noiseSpeedThreshold` | {{ "%.1f"|format(s.noise_speed_threshold) }} m/s | target speed counted as "loud" |
| `memorySeconds`       | {{ "%.1f"|format(s.memory_seconds) }}s | how long a lost target keeps being searched |
{% if s.squad_alert_radius > 0 %}| `squadAlertRadius`    | {{ "%.1f"|format(s.squad_alert_radius) }}m | same-archetype allies alerted the instant this AI notices the target — see `AlertSquad()`/`ReceiveAllyAlert()` |
